          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong Tambara-Yamagami
            (TY) category is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fusion+category"} fusion category
            that may be regarded as a non-trivial extension of a category of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+spaces"} graded vector spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
            = succeed "-graded" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            In 2-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            (QFT), a TY category is thought to encode as a
            %em symmetry category
            what is nowadays known as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-invertible+symmetry"} non-invertible symmetry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            of the category correspond to line
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/defects"} defects
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A Tambara-Yamagami category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi TY
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TY(G)
            is defined as follows.
          %p
            Starting from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I=G\coprod \{m\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi TY
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TY(G)
            by defining the simple objects as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi g
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_g\}_{g\in G}\coprod \{U_m\}
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi g
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi gg
                        %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{g}\otimes U_{g'}=U_{gg'}
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi g
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi m
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{g}\otimes U_m = U_m
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi m
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi g
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_m\otimes U_g = U_m
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi m
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi m
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_m\otimes U_m = \sum_{g\in G} U_g
          %p
            Unless stated otherwise, we assume the ground field of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi TY
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TY(G)
            to be
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#PlavnikSanfordSconce2023"} Plavnik &amp; Sanford &amp; Sconce 2023
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            It was shown by
            %a{:href => "#Tambara1998tensor"} Tambara &amp; Yamagami (1998)
            that these categories are classified by pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi χ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\chi,\tau)
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi:G\times G\to \mathbb{C}^*
            a bicharacter, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            a square root of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{|G|}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
              is symmetric and nondegenerate,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi TY
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TY(G)
              exists only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is abelian.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi TY
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TY(G)
              is not necessarily unique for a choice of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi TY
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TY(G)
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "unitary+fusion+category"} unitary fusion category
          %p
            This follows from (
            %a{:href => "#GalindoHongRowell2013"}> Galindo &amp; Hong &amp; Rowell 2013, theorem 5.20
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi TY
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TY(G)
              is a braided fusion category if and only if
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ≅
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\cong\mathbb{Z}_{2}^{n}
          %p
            The above is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Siehler2000"}> Siehler 2000, theorem 1.2(1)
            ).
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi TY
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TY(\mathbb{Z}_{2})
                is realised by two distinct unitary fusion categories (distinguished by the Frobenius-Schur indicator
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϰ
                        %mi m
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varkappa_{m}\in\{+1,-1\}
                of
                = succeed ")," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4
                distinct braidings. All
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 8
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 8
                of these unitary braided fusion categories (UBFCs) are
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "modular+tensor+category"} modular
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϰ
                        %mi m
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varkappa_{m}=+1
                are known as the Ising categories, while two of the UBFCs with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϰ
                        %mi m
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varkappa_{m}=-1
                describe
                %a{:href => "su2-anyon"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
                  \-anyons
                at level
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k=2
            %li
              %p
                As worked out in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#Tambara1998tensor"} Tambara &amp; Yamagami (1998)
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi TY
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TY(\mathbb{Z}_2\times\mathbb{Z}_2)
                = succeed ")," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi τ
                        %mo =
                        %mo ±
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau=\pm\frac{1}{2}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                      %mo =
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau=\frac{1}{2}
                and trivial bicharacter,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi TY
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TY
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+representations"} category of representations
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dihedral+group"} dihedral group
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_8
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau=-\frac{1}{2}
                and trivial character, this is the representation category of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternion+group"} quaternion group
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Q
                          %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_8
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                      %mo =
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau=\frac{1}{2}
                and nontrivial character, this is the representation category of the Kac-Paljutkin 8-dimensional
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebra"} Hopf algebra
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tannaka+duality"} Tannaka duality
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#PlavnikSanfordSconce2023
              %p
                Julia Plavnik, Sean Sanford, Dalton Sconce,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Tambara-Yamagami Categories over the Reals: The Non-Split Case
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.17843"} arXiv:2303.17843
            %li#GalindoHongRowell2013
              %p
                Cesar Galindo, Seung-Moon Hong,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Rowell"} Eric Rowell
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generalized and Quasi-Localizations of Braid Group Representations
                %strong 2013(3)
                (2013) 693-731 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/imrn/rnr269"}> doi:10.1093/imrn/rnr269
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Siehler2000
              %p
                Jacob Siehler,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Braided Near-Group Categories
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0011037"} arXiv:0011037
            %li#AnyonWiki
              %p
                AnyonWiki,
                %a{:href => "http://www.thphys.nuim.ie/AnyonWiki/index.php/List_of_small_multiplicity-free_fusion_rings"} List of small multiplicity-free fusion rings
          %h3#general General
          %p Original articles:
          %ul
            %li#Tambara1998tensor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daisuke+Tambara"}> Daisuke Tambara
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shigeru+Yamagami"} Shigeru Yamagami
              = succeed "," do
                %em Tensor categories with fusion rules of self-duality for finite abelian groups
              %strong 209
              (1998) 692-707 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1006/jabr.1998.7558"}> doi:10.1006/jabr.1998.7558
              \&amp;rbrack;
